    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §6-p, Bank L; add §354-f, Exec L; add §29-a, Veterans' Services L",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8670\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the banking law and the executive law, in relation to\ncertain notices and services upon application for a mortgage guaranteed\nunder the \"Servicemen's Readjustment Act of 1944\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to ensure that prospective homebuyers\nwho are veterans are provided the opportunity to receive educational\nservices to protect their financial interests.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. amends the banking law by adding a new section 6-p to provide\nnotice of the availability of loan counseling for mortgages guaranteed\nby the Servicemen's Readjustment Act of 1944 at the time of applica-\ntions.\n\nSection 2. amends the executive law by adding a new section 354-f to\nprovide loan counseling for mortgages guaranteed by the Servicemen's\nReadjustment Act of 1944.\n\nSection 3. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhen applying for Veterans Affairs (VA) home loans Veterans are often\ntargeted by unscrupulous mortgage brokers and loan companies. This\nlegislation will provide that prospective homebuyers are offered accu-\nrate and educational information to ensure that they obtain financing\nthat is fair, honest and tailored to their individual needs.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred twentieth day after it\nshall have become a law.\n",
